sequenceDiagram
    participant App as App<br>[implements GapPeripheralResponse]
    participant Node as Node<br>[implements GapPeripheral]
    participant Central as BLE Central

    Note over Node, Central: Messages between Node and BLE Central<br>are link-layer events, not driven by the App.<br>The App only observes them through<br>Echo callbacks (e.g. CurrentState).

    Central-)Node: Pairing_Request (MITM requested)
    Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.AuthenticationRequired(<br>isNumericComparison=true, passkey=485923)

    Note over App: Display passkey. User compares with the central's display.

    alt User confirms match
        App->>Node: GapPeripheral.NumericComparisonConfirm(true)
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.NumberOfBondsChanged(1)
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.PairingResult(pairedSuccessfully=true)
    else User rejects
        App->>Node: GapPeripheral.NumericComparisonConfirm(false)
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.PairingResult(<br>pairedSuccessfully=false, reason=numericComparisonFailed)
    else Timeout (30s SMP timeout, no confirm)
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.PairingResult(<br>pairedSuccessfully=false, reason=timeout)
    else Central disconnects before confirm
        rect rgb(245, 230, 230)
            Central-)Node: LL_TERMINATE_IND
        end
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.CurrentState(standby)
        Note over App, Node: If the central disconnects before the App confirms,<br>PairingResult may or may not fire before CurrentState(standby).<br>Reason: SMP is paused waiting on the local user response,<br>so the stack has no canonical cancellation event to raise.<br>Treat CurrentState(standby) as terminal.
    end
